lq3 QOP-MG build: release the file-scope gauge field of chroma's QOP-MG LinOp solver after use.

Applied by build_qopmg.sh (fetch) to builds/chroma-cpu-lq3-qopmg/src/chroma only (patch -p1 in the chroma
tree), never to the base build's source.

lib/actions/ferm/invert/qop_mg/syssolver_linop_qop_mg_w.cc keeps `static multi1d<LatticeColorMatrix> u`
at file scope so that its peekpoke0..3 callbacks can read the links while MGP(initialize) builds the QDP/C
gauge field (QDP_M_eq_func, other_libs/wilsonmg/lib/wilsonmg_p.c:196, the only use; MGP(solve) and the
rest of the bridge never call them). The copy then stays alive until program exit, where its destructor
runs after QDP++ has torn down its allocator's pointer map: QDP::Allocator::delete_aligned ->
std::map::erase on the destroyed map. Job 1365333: every run that constructed a QOP-MG solver (chroma
propagator on 2 and 4 ranks, hmc with the MdagM solver, which builds LinOp solvers inside) finished its
work, printed its results, and then died at exit with "free(): invalid next size" (SIGABRT) or SIGSEGV
in ~multi1d<LatticeColorMatrix> (addr2line on both binaries). Results were right (hmc vs QPhiX CG:
deltaH and all 32 force records agree); only the exit failed, which fails the job and the test.

Fix: u.resize(0) right after MGP(initialize). The four lattice fields are freed while QDP++ is alive and
the static is left as an empty array, whose destructor touches no lattice memory. It also drops one gauge
field per rank that otherwise lived for the whole run.

--- a/lib/actions/ferm/invert/qop_mg/syssolver_linop_qop_mg_w.cc
+++ b/lib/actions/ferm/invert/qop_mg/syssolver_linop_qop_mg_w.cc
@@ -132,6 +132,11 @@
       void (*peekpoke[4])(QLA(ColorMatrix) *dest, int coords[]) =
         {peekpoke0,peekpoke1,peekpoke2,peekpoke3};
       MGP(initialize)(machsize, latsize, peekpoke);
+      // lq3 patch: the peekpoke functions read u only inside MGP(initialize)
+      // (QDP_M_eq_func, wilsonmg_p.c), so release it now. Kept, this file-scope
+      // static is destroyed at exit after QDP++ has shut down its allocator and
+      // every chroma/hmc run that used QOP-MG crashed there (job 1365333).
+      u.resize(0);
 	
 	//MGP(teststuff)();
     }
